  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...A Nor'easter brings below normal temperatures, breezy \nconditions, and gusty winds through this weekend. \n\nA Nor'easter will develop off the east coast this evening before \ntracking north towards New England. The proximity of the Nor'easter \nwill bring increased cloud cover, below normal temperatures, \nand breezy conditions to the area through the weekend. Surface \nhigh pressure to the west will maintain dry conditions locally, \nalthough the tight pressure gradient will result in gusty winds \ndaily. Cloud cover decreases overnight, with conditions \nfavorable for radiational cooling leading to a Frost Advisory \nbeing issued for the Alleghenies. While most of the area will \ndip into the 40s, higher elevations will see temperatures in the\n30s. Temperatures as low as 33 degrees in the Alleghenies will \nresult in frost formation. Below normal temperatures continue \nthrough the weekend with highs in the upper 60s to 70s and \novernight lows in the 40s and 50s.\n\nEnsemble guidance continues to show a good bit of uncertainty \nregarding the exact track of the Nor'easter as it tracks offshore. \nSome solutions have the track further south and west, leading to \ngustier winds and potentially increased precipitation chances. \nWhile model guidance trended westward overnight, models this \nmorning have backed off leading to continued uncertainty. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Warm and calm conditions next week before rainfall \nchances return by late next week.\n\nAs this Nor'easter advances further offshore, an upper level ridge \nbuilds over the Great Plains bringing higher pressure, calmer winds, \nand predominantly dry condtions to our region. A few showers could \nlinger across northern Maryland Monday morning should this \nweekend's Nor'easter track further west. Mid-level ridging \nbuilding over the Midwest continues to raise daily temperatures \nthroughout the week, warming into above-normal temperatures by \nthe end of the week. \n\nA low pressure system advancing out of the Midwest brings humid \nconditions and chances for showers back to our region late next \nweek.",
